<http://data.silknow.org/object/a9b042ec-0944-3266-822e-41272a076fad/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Bicolour damask with satin ground and “jaspé” (mottled hank dyed warp). This is a special dyeing process in which the hank is introduced into the dye only once; the material thus gains a mottled effect, whith different shades of the same colour. The fabric is structured geometrically: the space is divided by an S-shaped ogival pattern, interrupted by crowns; in the interior of the spaces there are tulips which show a Turkish influence, ans stylized plants. One of the selvedges is preserved, in pink and white."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/a9b042ec-0944-3266-822e-41272a076fad> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/a9b042ec-0944-3266-822e-41272a076fad>
